      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A room map shows several possible starting points, and reception can ask about visitors’ interests.\", \"decision\": \"How should visitors choose a starting room?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nReception asks about visitors’ interests before pointing out a starting room on the map. The suggested start follows the visitor’s stated curiosity.\nVisitors mark a preferred starting room on the map, and reception offers any useful context. Visitors make the initial choice before receiving guidance.\nReception offers several starting rooms on the map and asks visitors which interests them. Concrete choices help visitors express a preference."
    }
